# Line-ending policy for a Keil / Chinese-locale embedded project.
# The .c/.h sources are GBK(CP936) + CRLF on purpose (Keil on a zh-CN machine).
# Never let git normalize them: an EOL rewrite plus an encoding-losing editor is how
# Chinese comments get destroyed. Binary-ish project files likewise stay byte-exact.
*.c             -text
*.h             -text
*.s             -text
*.uvprojx       -text
*.uvoptx        -text
*.dbgconf       -text
*.scvd          -text
*.axf           binary
*.hex           -text
*.map           -text
*.lst           -text

# Plain text that SHOULD be normalized to LF in the repository.
*.md            text eol=lf
*.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Windows batch needs CRLF on disk.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
